# Controls what `railway up` UPLOADS, separate from (and more important than) .dockerignore — that
# file only prunes the build context AFTER Railway already has it; without this, `railway up` falls
# back to the much sparser root .gitignore, which excludes node_modules/.env but nothing else here.
# A real `railway up` against that fallback tried to upload 378MB and was rejected outright (413 Payload
# Too Large) — this repo's local-only build artifacts (desktop installers, Android build output, a
# project's actual video files) dwarf the studios/vcut SOURCE this deploy actually needs.
#
# Deliberately mirrors .dockerignore's own exclusion list byte-for-byte rather than drifting
# independently — see that file's own doc comments for the full reasoning (pnpm workspace discovery
# needing every member's package.json, the recursive-glob/permission-bit/junction gotchas already
# fought there). Keep the two in sync; there's no single source both could point at without turning
# one into a symlink of the other, which Windows checkouts of this repo can't rely on.

